• Services by a Provider which were pre-paid by the Covered Person by virtue of a discount 
program, coupon, retail or online offer; 
• short term storage and retrieval for cord blood, breast milk, and other materials, except as 
specifically identified as covered; 
• social Services, 
• transportation, except as otherwise covered under the Plan; 
• removal of skin tags; 
• Services provided under a direct primary care agreement; 
• replacement of lost, broken, destroyed or stolen Covered Prescription Drug Products 
within the Covered Person’s control. One fill per year may be allowed, per medication; 
• over-the-counter supplies, devices, tests, medications and non-prescription medications 
